              where
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the left square is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %li
                %p
                  the bottom left morphism is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            %p Then the right square is a pullback iff the total rectangle is.
          (e.g.
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Gran21"} Gran 2021, Lem. 1.15
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#CarboniJanelidzeKellyParé97"} Carboni, Janelidze, Kelly and Paré 1997, Lemma 4.6
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#GarnerLack12"} Garner and Lack 2012, Lemma 2.2
          %p
            For a more general statement that holds in categories that are not necessarily
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular"} regular
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Przybylek13"} Przybylek (2013)
          %p
            Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WrongWayPastingLawInRegularCategory"}
            implies the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
          #ReversePastingLawForInfinityGroupoids.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (reverse pasting law for
                = succeed "-pullbacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-groupoids)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %br/
              The reverse pasting law (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WrongWayPastingLawInRegularCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoids
              as soon as the bottom left morphism is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                  effective epimorphism in this
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              and using the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              where both bottom morphisms are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            %p Now observe that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an effective epimorphism of
                  = succeed "-groupoids" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
                  (by
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a{:href => "effective+epimorphism+in+an+infinity1-category#EffectiveEpisOfInfinityGroupoids"} this Prop.
              %li
                %p
                  a Kan fibration which resolves a surjection on connected components is degreewise surjective (by
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a{:href => "Kan+fibration#EveryPiZeroEpiIsResolvedByASurjectiveKanFibration"} this Prop.
              %li
                %p
                  a degreewise surjection of simplicial sets is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  (by
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a{:href => "SimpSet#EpimorphismsOfSimplicialSetsDetectedDegreewise"} this Prop.
                %p
                  hence is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
                  in a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                  (since
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                  is a
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %p
              Hence the bottom left morphism in our diagram of simplicial sets is a regular epimorphism and the claim follows by Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WrongWayPastingLawInRegularCategory"}
